/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'none'

# Everything Astro content-hashes. The hash is derived from the file's own
# bytes, so a changed file is a changed URL and a cached copy of the old one can
# never be stale — which is the only condition under which `immutable` is safe.
#
# The rule sets no header the `/*` block above sets. That matters on Cloudflare
# Pages, which joins same-named headers from every matching rule with a comma
# rather than choosing the most specific: two rules setting `Cache-Control`
# would emit both values. Overriding an inherited header needs an explicit
# `! Header-Name`. `tests/deployment.test.ts` gates exactly that.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Deliberately NOT listed: `/pagefind/*`.
#
# Only two of its four asset classes are content-hashed. `pagefind/index/*` and
# `pagefind/fragment/*` carry a hash; `pagefind-entry.json` and
# `wasm.*.pagefind` are stable-named and rewritten on every build. Marking the
# directory immutable would pin a returning reader's `pagefind-entry.json` to a
# year-old copy pointing at index chunks that no longer exist — search would
# break silently after the first republish, for exactly the readers who visit
# most often. The platform default (`public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` plus an
# `ETag`) revalidates cheaply and is correct for all four.
#
# Also not listed: HTML and the JSON data files. Requirements section 20 asks
# for a short cache or revalidation for HTML and a short cache with `ETag` for
# JSON, and Cloudflare Pages already serves precisely that by default on every
# 200. A rule restating the platform default would be one more thing to keep in
# sync with it.
